1	//! The framing planner (road map "creator-jobs" VR2a1, spec §11 VR-20,
2	//! VR-22, VR-23): a clip's analysed subjects in, a [`FramingPath`] out — a
3	//! similarity per instant from the canvas the clip was authored for (`Ws ×
4	//! Hs`) to the current one (`W × H`). Pure; nothing here edits.
5	//! `edit_reframe.rs`'s op writes the path as the clip's base and actions
6	//! (`reframe_cover.rs`).
7	//!
8	//! **The frames.** A box is 0…1 of the upright picture from its top-left. Its
9	//! point `(bx, by)` is `u = (bx·mw − mw/2, by·mh − mh/2)` px from the
10	//! UNCROPPED centre (`mw × mh` the media's displayed size), and lands on the
11	//! source canvas at `anchor + s·u` — `edit_zoom.rs`'s (★) at θ = 0, with
12	//! `anchor` and `s` the clip's base `video`. A crop moves only the
13	//! picture's extent, the cropped rect `anchor + s·(c ± (cw/2, ch/2))`, so
14	//! the analysis cache never depends on it.
15	//!
16	//! **The window.** The part of the source canvas the target shows: `W/k ×
17	//! H/k`, where `k·s` is `zoom ×` the fill scale of the cropped picture on
18	//! the target (`Project::fill_scale`), at most `SCALE_MAX`. A key is
19	//! `(k, dx, dy)` with `dx = k·(Ws/2 − wc.x)`, `dy = k·(Hs/2 − wc.y)` for a
20	//! window centred at `wc`; composed into a placement as `scale′ = k·scale,
21	//! x′ = k·x + dx, y′ = k·y + dy` (VR-3, VR-27). Every `wc` is clamped so the
22	//! window lies inside the cropped rect (VR-7's covering key).
23	//!
24	//! **The placement in force** (VR-27 (a)). A clip with actions moves its
25	//! picture under the window: a sample's point is (★) through the clip's
26	//! evaluated placement at its own tick (`Frame.placed`), and the rect the
27	//! window is clamped into is the COMMON one — the cropped rects of the base
28	//! and of the placement at every action's end, intersected — with `k`
29	//! raised until the window fits it, held so `k·s` stays at most `SCALE_MAX`
30	//! at every one of those placements. A clip with no actions is VR2a2's.
31	//!
32	//! **The path.** VR-21 (`reframe_tracks.rs`) chooses a subject per sample;
33	//! VR-22 composes the window on it; `reframe_path.rs` writes the keys —
34	//! VR-23's moves only when the median-filtered subject leaves a dead zone,
35	//! each a hold key and an eased key, and VR-24's hard cuts, loss, return and
36	//! two people — snapped to the canvas's frames. Where there is nothing to
37	//! follow the path holds a `where_empty` state ([`WhereEmpty`]): the window on
38	//! the cropped centre, or the whole cropped picture fitted (`edit_zoom.rs`'s
39	//! solves at θ = 0), which [`fixed_framing`] also answers for `follow`
40	//! `center` and `fit` (VR2a2).
41	
42	use crate::clip_source_time::{clip_time_of_source, in_played_window, Round};
43	use crate::edit_zoom::{zoom_offset, zoom_scale, ZoomFit, ZoomRegion};
44	use crate::model::{Clip, Curve, MediaKind, Project, Source};
45	use crate::props_check::SCALE_MAX;
46	use crate::reframe_path::write_keys;
47	pub use crate::reframe_subjects::Subjects;
48	pub use crate::reframe_tracks::{
49	    choose_subject, Chosen, Follow, SubjectBox, SubjectKind, SubjectSample,
50	};
51	use crate::time::Ticks;
52	use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};
